12. In his cross-examination done by the Ld. counsel for the respondent no.1 and 2,
PW-1 stated inter alia that he met with an accident near Udyog Nagar station by an ambulance; that the accident occurred at around 9.30 pm; that there was darkness on the spot of accident; that he was walking along the subway path;
that he was in conscious state after the accident for few minutes; that he was taken to the hospital in the very ambulance which was driven by driver Rajbir; that when he reached the hospital, he was unconscious; that where his accident occurred, there was no red light and it was a free traffic zone and he was standing to cross the road.

For this purpose, the Claims Tribunal and the Courts normally consider the nature of injury;
the part of the body where the injuries were sustained, surgeries, if any, underwent by the victim, confinement in the hospital and the duration of treatment".
37. Petitioner / injured had suffered grievous injuries including permanent disability due to the accident in question.
